<article> <header class="hero"> <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"> <a href="/">Home</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <a href="/glossary">Glossary</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <span>pacs.008</span> </nav> <div class="hero-badge"><span class="pulse-dot"></span><span style="position:relative;z-index:1">Glossary · Messages</span></div> <h1><span class="accent">pacs.008</span></h1> <p class="page-meta">Glossary entry · Last reviewed 26 July 2026</p> <!-- ANSWER BLOCK — picked up by speakable schema --> <p class="answer-block"><strong>pacs.008 (FIToFICustomerCreditTransfer)</strong> is the ISO 20022 message that carries a customer credit transfer between financial institutions — the MX successor to the MT 103. The current CBPR+ production version is <strong>pacs.008.001.08</strong>, and from 15 November 2026 its <code>&lt;PstlAdr&gt;</code> blocks must be fully structured or hybrid.</p> </header> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">In Practice</div> <h2 class="section-title">How pacs.008 works in practice</h2> <div class="content-block"><p>pacs.008 carries <code>&lt;PstlAdr&gt;</code> for the Debtor, Creditor and any Ultimate parties; agents are identified by BICFI rather than address. It is the inter-PSP payment message for SEPA SCT, SCT Inst and OCT Inst, and its R-transactions (pacs.004, camt.056, camt.029 and others) reference its original party data.</p></div> <p class="src">Source: the ioNova Postal Address Specification v2.0 (message versions; pacs.008.001.08 per IS2-100, 13 Dec 2024); §9 (SCT message flows); §13 (R-transactions).</p> <div class="content-block"><p>A creditor block inside pacs.008 with a hybrid address:</p></div>
<div class="code-block"><pre><span class="tag">&lt;CdtTrfTxInf&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;Cdtr&gt;</span>
    <span class="tag">&lt;Nm&gt;</span>Mohammed Ali Trading Co<span class="tag">&lt;/Nm&gt;</span>
    <span class="tag">&lt;PstlAdr&gt;</span>
      <span class="tag">&lt;PstCd&gt;</span>6011<span class="tag">&lt;/PstCd&gt;</span>
      <span class="tag">&lt;TwnNm&gt;</span>WELLINGTON<span class="tag">&lt;/TwnNm&gt;</span>
      <span class="tag">&lt;Ctry&gt;</span>NZ<span class="tag">&lt;/Ctry&gt;</span>
      <span class="tag">&lt;AdrLine&gt;</span>169 CUBA STREET<span class="tag">&lt;/AdrLine&gt;</span>
    <span class="tag">&lt;/PstlAdr&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;/Cdtr&gt;</span>
<span class="tag">&lt;/CdtTrfTxInf&gt;</span></pre></div> <div class="content-block"><p>Parent reference: <a href="/address-intelligence/structured-address-mandate">ISO 20022 deadline — the structured address mandate</a>.</p></div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">Citations</div> <h2 class="section-title">Sources</h2> <div class="sources-list"> <h3 class="sources-subhead">Standards &amp; regulatory sources</h3>
